h="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pierre Buyoya</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pierre Buyoya was a Tutsi army officer who twice seized power in Burundi, ruling from 1987 to 1993 and again from 1996 to 2003.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-chanel"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-chanel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pierre Chanel</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pierre Chanel (1803–1841) was a French Catholic priest of the Marist order who landed on Futuna in 1837 as one of the first missionaries in the western Pacific.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-corneille"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-corneille.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pierre Corneille</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pierre Corneille was a French dramatist, one of the three great playwrights of seventeenth-century France with Molière and Racine.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-daubusson"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-daubusson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pierre d'Aubusson</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pierre d'Aubusson was Grand Master of the Knights Hospitaller from 1476 to 1503.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-de-breze"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-de-breze.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pierre de Brézé</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pierre de Brézé was a French nobleman, soldier and leading adviser of Charles VII, grand seneschal of Normandy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="