gest sanctuary of the ancient Samnites.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pietrera-tumulus"><span class="enc-name">Pietrera Tumulus</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Pietrera Tumulus is a monumental Etruscan burial mound at Vetulonia in Tuscany, built in the 7th century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pietro-badoglio"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/pietro-badoglio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pietro Badoglio</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pietro Badoglio was an Italian marshal and politician.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pietro-doria"><span class="enc-name">Pietro Doria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pietro Doria (died 1380) was a Genoese admiral during the War of Chioggia against Venice.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pietro-gasparri"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/pietro-gasparri.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pietro Gasparri</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pietro Gasparri was an Italian cardinal, canon lawyer and diplomat of the Holy See.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pietro-giannone"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/pietro-giannone.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pietro Giannone</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pietro Giannone (1676–1748) was a Neapolitan jurist and historian.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pietro-i-candiano"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/pietro-i-candiano.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pietro I Candiano</span><span class="enc-type">Per