><span class="enc-snip">The Pindus is the main mountain range of mainland Greece, running southwards from the Albanian border between Epirus and Thessaly.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pinedjem-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/pinedjem-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pinedjem I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pinedjem I was High Priest of Amun at Thebes from about 1070 to 1032 BCE, during the Twenty-first Dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pineios-elis"><span class="enc-name">Pineios (Elis)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Pineios is a river of Elis in the north-western Peloponnese of Greece, flowing west from the Erymanthos mountains to the Ionian Sea.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pineios-thessaly"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/pineios-thessaly.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pineios (Thessaly)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Pineios, ancient Peneus, is the main river of Thessaly in Greece, about 200 kilometres long.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pinerolo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/pinerolo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pinerolo</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Pinerolo is a town in Piedmont, Italy, south-west of Turin at the entrance to the valleys leading to the French Alps.</span></a></li></ul>
